  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Given a scripted hand in which the user made 4 decisions, When its record is read, Then it holds 4 decision entries in order, each with street, the user's action, recommended action, equity %, required equity %, basis, explanation and grade [REQ-052.2]",
      "checked": false
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "Given a decision computed with an opponent's observed stats at 29 hands that reach 30 hands when the hand ends, When the record is read, Then its recommendation and numbers equal the advice computed from the decision-time snapshot [REQ-052.2]",
      "checked": false
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "Given a decision made without asking for a hint, When the record is read, Then its hinted flag is false [REQ-052.2]",
      "checked": false
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "Given a hand in which the user folded preflop at the first decision, When its record is read, Then it holds exactly 1 decision entry with its grade [REQ-052.2]",
      "checked": false
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "Given a graded decision, When the hand record is saved, Then the stored grade data is decided and documented (full GradeResult or grade, ruleId and marginPts plus a recommendation reference) and round-trips through JSON unchanged",
      "checked": false
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "Given an observed-stats snapshot built at a decision point that contains a null entry or a seat that is not a whole number from 1 to 10 (the table seat bound), When advice is computed from it, Then estimateOpponentRanges throws the documented RangeError (never a TypeError) and the bad seat is never silently ignored",
      "checked": false
    }
  ],
